<title>CHINA: Group forms for Pusan Bank $60 mln FRN.</title>
<headline>Group forms for Pusan Bank $60 mln FRN.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group has formed for Pusan Bank's US$60 million floating-rate notes due 2000, bookrunner BA Asia said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The three-year notes have annual put and call options.</p>
<p>They were issued at par to float at 50 basis points over the three-month London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>With fees, the all-in return for participants is 62.5 basis points.</p>
<p>Arrangers and lead managers, with US$10 million each, are BA Asia, Baring Brothers Ltd as agent for ING Baring Bank, Credit Suisse First Boston, IBJ Asia, Swiss Bank Corp and Standard Chartered Capital Markets.</p>
<p>The payment date is July 25.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
